  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieved 0.650 acc / 0.628 F1, a large jump over config_004 (same encoder, singleprofile) at 0.520, confirming that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is highly beneficial for scvi-encoded RNA. However, the aggregation choice within the multiprofile setting remains untested. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool when paired with scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting? This is a clean single-variable comparison (only aggregation changes from config_005). Why this is the best next experiment: It directly exploits the strongest positive signal in the search so far, isolates the aggregation design decision, and will either (a) yield a stronger RNA baseline for subsequent multimodal experiments or (b) confirm that simple avgpool is sufficient, redirecting budget toward other design axes (encoder choice, multimodal fusion) with greater confidence."
}

